{"id":"15e11a9a63f56ef5","group":"58","path":"58/batch01/58-thm-lebesgue-measure-regularity.md","title":"Lebesgue Measure Regularity","display":"thm-lebesgue-measure-regularity — Lebesgue Measure Regularity","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-lebesgue-measure-regularity","aliases":["58-thm-lebesgue-measure-regularity","Lebesgue Measure Regularity"],"display":"thm-lebesgue-measure-regularity — Lebesgue Measure Regularity","depends_on":["[[../batch02/58-df-standard-real-topology.md]]","[[../batch10/58-df-lebesgue]]","[[../batch02/58-df-open-set]]","[[../batch05/58-df-compact]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-lebesgue-measure-regularity"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-lebesgue-measure-regularity</span><span>Lebesgue Measure Regularity</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-lebesgue-measure-regularity — Lebesgue Measure Regularity"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"3b5b3d48ff1ff369\" href=\"?note=3b5b3d48ff1ff369\" title=\"../batch02/58-df-standard-real-topology.md\">../batch02/58-df-standard-real-topology.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"68427bc628af9b8d\" href=\"?note=68427bc628af9b8d\" title=\"../batch10/58-df-lebesgue\">../batch10/58-df-lebesgue</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"c664c247a9331632\" href=\"?note=c664c247a9331632\" title=\"../batch02/58-df-open-set\">../batch02/58-df-open-set</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"050f6d05b2c94aea\" href=\"?note=050f6d05b2c94aea\" title=\"../batch05/58-df-compact\">../batch05/58-df-compact</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\lambda\">\\(\\lambda\\)</span> (Lebesgue measure on <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb R\">\\(\\mathbb R\\)</span>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal L\">\\(\\mathcal L\\)</span> (Lebesgue sigma-algebra)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{LebesgueMeasure}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{LebesgueMeasure}_S\\)</span> (Lebesgue-measure predicate from dependency)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{LebesgueMeasurable}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{LebesgueMeasurable}_S\\)</span> (Lebesgue-measurability predicate from dependency)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal T_{\\mathbb R}\">\\(\\mathcal T_{\\mathbb R}\\)</span> (usual topology of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb R\">\\(\\mathbb R\\)</span>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Open}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Open}_S\\)</span> (open-set predicate)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Compact}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Compact}_S\\)</span> (compact-space predicate)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{SubspaceTopology}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{SubspaceTopology}_S\\)</span> (subspace-topology relation defined below)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{StandardRealTopology}_S(\\mathcal T_{\\mathbb R})\">\\(\\mathrm{StandardRealTopology}_S(\\mathcal T_{\\mathbb R})\\)</span>（see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"3b5b3d48ff1ff369\" href=\"?note=3b5b3d48ff1ff369\" title=\"../batch02/58-df-standard-real-topology.md\">../batch02/58-df-standard-real-topology.md</a>）。</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}subspace\\text{-}topology\\text{-}for\\text{-}regularity}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{SubspaceTopology}_S(\\tau_K,K,\\mathbb R,\\mathcal T_{\\mathbb R})\n\\leftrightarrow\nK\\subseteq\\mathbb R\\land\n\\tau_K=\\{U\\cap K\\mid U\\in\\mathcal T_{\\mathbb R}\\}.\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}subspace\\text{-}topology\\text{-}for\\text{-}regularity}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{SubspaceTopology}_S(\\tau_K,K,\\mathbb R,\\mathcal T_{\\mathbb R})\n\\leftrightarrow\nK\\subseteq\\mathbb R\\land\n\\tau_K=\\{U\\cap K\\mid U\\in\\mathcal T_{\\mathbb R}\\}.\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}lebesgue\\text{-}measure\\text{-}regularity}\\ \\vdash\\\n\\forall A\\subseteq\\mathbb R\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{LebesgueMeasure}_S(\\lambda,\\mathcal L,\\mathbb R)\n\\land\\mathrm{StandardRealTopology}_S(\\mathcal T_{\\mathbb R})\\land\\mathrm{LebesgueMeasurable}_S(A)\n\\to\n\\lambda(A)\n=\\sup\\bigl\\{\\lambda(K):K\\subseteq A\\land\n\\exists\\tau_K\\in V\\;(\n\\mathrm{SubspaceTopology}_S(\\tau_K,K,\\mathbb R,\\mathcal T_{\\mathbb R})\n\\land\\mathrm{Compact}_S(K,\\tau_K))\\bigr\\}\n=\\inf\\bigl\\{\\lambda(U):A\\subseteq U\\land\n\\mathrm{Open}_S(U,\\mathbb R,\\mathcal T_{\\mathbb R})\\bigr\\}\n\\Bigr).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}lebesgue\\text{-}measure\\text{-}regularity}\\ \\vdash\\\n\\forall A\\subseteq\\mathbb R\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{LebesgueMeasure}_S(\\lambda,\\mathcal L,\\mathbb R)\n\\land\\mathrm{StandardRealTopology}_S(\\mathcal T_{\\mathbb R})\\land\\mathrm{LebesgueMeasurable}_S(A)\n\\to\n\\lambda(A)\n=\\sup\\bigl\\{\\lambda(K):K\\subseteq A\\land\n\\exists\\tau_K\\in V\\;(\n\\mathrm{SubspaceTopology}_S(\\tau_K,K,\\mathbb R,\\mathcal T_{\\mathbb R})\n\\land\\mathrm{Compact}_S(K,\\tau_K))\\bigr\\}\n=\\inf\\bigl\\{\\lambda(U):A\\subseteq U\\land\n\\mathrm{Open}_S(U,\\mathbb R,\\mathcal T_{\\mathbb R})\\bigr\\}\n\\Bigr).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The measure variable is now tied to the canonical Lebesgue measure and sigma-algebra; the previous implication was false for an arbitrary function named <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\lambda\">\\(\\lambda\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>The first equality is inner regularity by compact sets; the second is outer regularity by open sets.</li>\n<li>The topology on each compact candidate is the actual subspace topology, rather than an undefined restriction of a family of open sets.</li>\n<li>The values are understood in <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"[0,\\infty]\">\\([0,\\infty]\\)</span>, so the statement also covers measurable sets of infinite measure.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch02/58-df-standard-real-topology.md","status":"resolved","id":"3b5b3d48ff1ff369","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch02/58-df-standard-real-topology.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch10/58-df-lebesgue","status":"resolved","id":"68427bc628af9b8d","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch10/58-df-lebesgue]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch02/58-df-open-set","status":"resolved","id":"c664c247a9331632","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch02/58-df-open-set]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch05/58-df-compact","status":"resolved","id":"050f6d05b2c94aea","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch05/58-df-compact]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch02/58-df-standard-real-topology.md","status":"resolved","id":"3b5b3d48ff1ff369","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{StandardRealTopology}_S(\\mathcal T_{\\mathbb R})$（see [[../batch02/58-df-standard-real-topology.md]]）。","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"\\lambda","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathbb R","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathcal L","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{LebesgueMeasure}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{LebesgueMeasurable}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathcal T_{\\mathbb R}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathbb R","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Open}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Compact}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{SubspaceTopology}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{StandardRealTopology}_S(\\mathcal T_{\\mathbb R})","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}subspace\\text{-}topology\\text{-}for\\text{-}regularity}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{SubspaceTopology}_S(\\tau_K,K,\\mathbb R,\\mathcal T_{\\mathbb R})\n\\leftrightarrow\nK\\subseteq\\mathbb R\\land\n\\tau_K=\\{U\\cap K\\mid U\\in\\mathcal T_{\\mathbb R}\\}.","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}lebesgue\\text{-}measure\\text{-}regularity}\\ \\vdash\\\n\\forall A\\subseteq\\mathbb R\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{LebesgueMeasure}_S(\\lambda,\\mathcal L,\\mathbb R)\n\\land\\mathrm{StandardRealTopology}_S(\\mathcal T_{\\mathbb R})\\land\\mathrm{LebesgueMeasurable}_S(A)\n\\to\n\\lambda(A)\n=\\sup\\bigl\\{\\lambda(K):K\\subseteq A\\land\n\\exists\\tau_K\\in V\\;(\n\\mathrm{SubspaceTopology}_S(\\tau_K,K,\\mathbb R,\\mathcal T_{\\mathbb R})\n\\land\\mathrm{Compact}_S(K,\\tau_K))\\bigr\\}\n=\\inf\\bigl\\{\\lambda(U):A\\subseteq U\\land\n\\mathrm{Open}_S(U,\\mathbb R,\\mathcal T_{\\mathbb R})\\bigr\\}\n\\Bigr).","display":true},{"tex":"\\lambda","display":false},{"tex":"[0,\\infty]","display":false}],"bytes":2463,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-4278","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch01/58-thm-lebesgue-measure-regularity.md|58-thm-lebesgue-measure-regularity]]（batch01）"},{"id":"7334957c6d59eacc","anchor":"ref-211","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[58-thm-0-sharp.md]]\n[[58-thm-L-condensation.md]]\n[[58-thm-L-definability.md]]\n[[58-thm-L-generic-extensio